# Daijin role configuration: NAMES ONLY, never values.
#
# Daijin does not read these variables itself. They are here because a role's `keyRef` is a
# POINTER, and this file documents the pointer forms and the names a pointer may target, so
# a reader can see what a configuration refers to without a key ever being written down.
#
# The rule this serves: no key value enters this repository, its settings files, its logs,
# or any RPC response. The value is fetched at the moment a provider call is made.
#
# POINTER FORMS, in `keyRef`:
#
#   env:NAME                   the key is in the environment variable NAME
#   file:/abs/path             the key is the contents of that file
#   env-file:/abs/path#NAME    NAME is read from a dotenv-style file; if NAME ends in _FILE
#                              its value is a PATH and the key is that file's contents
#
# A bare pointer is the legacy form and still works, disambiguated by shape: an absolute
# path is a file, a SHOUTING_NAME is an environment variable. Anything else is refused
# rather than guessed. New configuration should use a prefixed form.

# The four roles. Set these through settingsSet, not through this file.
#
# DAIJIN_ROLE_ENGINEER_KEYREF=env-file:/absolute/path/to/.env.local#ZAI_API_KEY_FILE
# DAIJIN_ROLE_ENGINEER_MODEL=
# DAIJIN_ROLE_ENGINEER_ENDPOINT=
#
# DAIJIN_ROLE_WATCHER_KEYREF=env-file:/absolute/path/to/.env.local#OPENROUTER_API_KEY_FILE
# DAIJIN_ROLE_WATCHER_MODEL=
# DAIJIN_ROLE_WATCHER_ENDPOINT=
#
# The teacher and the auditor stay unconfigured until their keys are supplied. An
# unconfigured role reads as keyResolvable null, which is "never configured" and is a
# different claim from false, which is "configured and unreachable".

# Names a pointer may target in the AI Brain Platform's own environment file. Values live
# outside that repository, in files with mode 0600; only the names appear here.
#
# ZAI_API_KEY_FILE                    engineer key, Z.AI direct
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY_FILE             OpenRouter key
# PROVIDER_ROUTER_SHARED_SECRET_FILE  shared secret for the local provider router

# The state root the daemon keeps machine state under. The index lives here after D-0031,
# keyed by the repo id in .daijin/manifest.json, and it is passed to serve-repo in the
# pasted MCP snippet so an agent launched under a different HOME still finds the index.
#
# DAIJIN_STATE_ROOT=
